      "text": "To determine which functions have inverses, we need to check if each function is one-to-one (injective). A function has an inverse if and only if it is one-to-one. A function is one-to-one if different inputs produce different outputs, i.e., if \\( f(a) = f(b) \\) whenever \\( a = b \\).\n\nHere are the graphs of the functions:\n\n1. Function A: Graphed as a cubic polynomial \\( f(x) = \\frac{x^3}{40} + \\frac{x^2}{20} - \\frac{x}{2} + 2 \\). This is a cubic polynomial, and all cubic polynomials are one-to-one. So, function A has an inverse.\n\n2. Function B: Graphed as a line \\( y = -3x - 5 \\). This is a linear function, and all linear functions are one-to-one. So, function B has an inverse.\n\n3. Function C: Graphed as a circle \\( x^2 + y^2 = 1 \\). This is a circle centered at the origin with radius 1. The circle is not one-to-one because it does not pass the horizontal line test (different x-values can give the same y-value). So, function C does not have an inverse.\n\n4. Function D: Graphed as a quarter circle \\( y = \\sqrt{1 - x^2} \\) for \\( -1 \\leq x \\leq 1 \\). This is a quarter of a circle in the first quadrant, which is one-to-one within this range. So, function D has an inverse.\n\n5. Function E: Graphed as a piecewise linear function defined by \\( y = \\frac{x^3}{40} + \\frac{x^2}{20} - \\frac{x}{2} + 2 \\) for \\( x \\geq 2 \\) and \\( y = x - 4 \\) for \\( x < 2 \\). This function is smooth and does not have a jump or a kink at all points, making it one-to-one. So, function E has an inverse.\n\nTherefore, the functions that have inverses are A, B, D, and E. The answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{A, B, D, E}\n\\]",
