      "text": "To determine which functions have inverses, we need to identify which functions are one-to-one. A function is one-to-one if every horizontal line intersects its graph at most once. This means that for any \\( y \\)-value, there is at most one \\( x \\)-value that maps to it.\n\nLet's analyze each function graphically.\n\n1. **Graph A**: The graph of function A consists of a parabola that opens upwards and has its vertex at \\((0, 2)\\). This graph is one-to-one because every horizontal line will intersect the graph at most once. Therefore, function A has an inverse.\n\n2. **Graph B**: The graph of function B consists of a parabola that opens upwards and has its vertex at \\((0, -2)\\). This graph is not one-to-one because for any \\( y \\)-value greater than \\(-2\\), there are two corresponding \\( x \\)-values that map to it. Therefore, function B does not have an inverse.\n\n3. **Graph C**: The graph of function C consists of a semicircle with its center at the origin and a radius of 4. This graph is one-to-one because every horizontal line will intersect the graph at most once. Therefore, function C has an inverse.\n\n4. **Graph D**: The graph of function D is a circle centered at the origin with a radius of \\( \\sqrt{5} \\). This graph is not one-to-one because for any \\( x \\)-value in the interval \\([- \\sqrt{5}, \\sqrt{5}]\\), there are two corresponding \\( y \\)-values that map to it. Therefore, function D does not have an inverse.\n\n5. **Graph E**: The graph of function E is a cubic function \\( y = \\frac{x^3}{40} + \\frac{x^2}{20} - \\frac{x}{2} + 2 \\). This graph is one-to-one because the function is strictly increasing over its entire domain. Therefore, function E has an inverse.\n\nFrom the analysis above, the functions that have inverses are A, C, and E. Therefore, the answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{A, C, E}\n\\]",
